From 15f4fddd4950b2f89fa32eec74b43c19d81b5a27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:08:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/51] Fix preview-to-playback size mismatch, split paddings
 and per-layer opacity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The bilingual subtitle view covers the whole player surface including
letterbox bars, and its font size was computed against that full
height. In portrait playback the raw view height is roughly double the
video area, so subtitles came out far larger than the style editor
preview (which assumed a 640x400 landscape reference). The player now
feeds the view the video aspect ratio, and the font size and the
bottom anchor are computed against the video area carved out of the
view — identical to fullscreen playback and to the preview, which also
moved to a 16:9 640x360 reference.

The single padding setting also tied the horizontal padding to the
vertical one (always half of it). It is now two independent sliders
(0-16 dp each); the legacy single value migrates to vertical = old,
horizontal = old / 2, which is exactly what it used to render.

The original-text opacity only affected the first (original) layer.
Each layer now has its own opacity slider (30-100%), so whichever
language ends up on either line can be dimmed independently.
